.TH STR_IS_PALINDROME 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
str_is_palindrome \- check whether a string is a palindrome
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int str_is_palindrome(const char *" str );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B str_is_palindrome()
function checks whether
.I str
reads the same forwards and backwards.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 if
.I str
is a palindrome, 0 otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
int result = str_is_palindrome("madam");
/* result is 1 */
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Haseeb
